============
Rate Limiter with Spring Boot + Bucket4j.
Architecture :

1.Client :->Sends GET /api/products
2.Spring Security Filter Chain :->Controls the request flow
3.RateLimitingFilter.java :->Identifies the client and checks the limit
4.RateLimitConfiguration.java + Bucket4j :->Creates and manages the client's bucket
  if (Allowed){
  Controller executes
  200 OK
 }else{
Rejected
Controller not executed
}

We use Bucket4j is a Java library that implements rate-limiting algorithms.
We chose the Token Bucket algorithm.

Working Steps:
-> HTTP Client
-> Spring Security Filter Chain
-> RateLimitFilter
-> Identifies client by IP
-> Bucket4j ->Checks and consumes tokens
-> RateLimiterController

Limitation of Version 1 :If we deploy our application on two servers.
And each server has its own ConcurrentHashMap.
Server A doesn't know what happened on Server B.
There is another limitation: our map can keep growing as new IP addresses appear.
We need a way to expire inactive buckets.
